# Example environment file -- PLACEHOLDERS ONLY.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in your own values. `.env` is git-ignored and must
# never be committed. Never paste real keys into this example file.
#
# Nothing in Phase 1 requires any of these: the Yahoo/yfinance development
# provider needs no credentials. They are listed so the Phase 2 Alpaca
# adapter has a documented, code-free home for its configuration.

# --- Alpaca (PAPER TRADING ONLY -- this project never trades real money) ---
ALPACA_API_KEY_ID=your-paper-key-id-here
ALPACA_API_SECRET_KEY=your-paper-secret-key-here
ALPACA_BASE_URL=https://paper-api.alpaca.markets
ALPACA_DATA_URL=https://data.alpaca.markets
# Free-tier data feed is "iex"; "sip" requires a paid subscription.
ALPACA_DATA_FEED=iex

# --- SEC EDGAR contact (Phase 8) ---
# The SEC asks automated clients to identify themselves with a contact address
# so it can reach whoever is generating traffic. This is contact identification,
# NOT an API secret -- EDGAR has no API key and needs no account.
#
# Without it the EDGAR source reports UNCONFIGURED and is switched off; Yahoo
# news keeps working. Replace the example address with your own.
SEC_USER_AGENT="AI-Market-Analysis your-email@example.com"

# --- Anthropic (OPTIONAL -- AI explanation of research evidence, Phase 11) ---
# Both variables are required together. With neither set, the AI explanation is
# switched off and nothing else changes: bars, features, hypotheses, the
# assessment, the market scan, news, feeds and paper positions all work exactly
# as before. Only the "Explain with AI" feature becomes unavailable.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is a real secret. Keep it out of this file, out of the
# repository and out of screenshots; `.env` is git-ignored.
#
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL has no default on purpose. Model identifiers change over
# time, and one hardcoded in the source would go stale quietly and then fail as
# though the service were down. Set it to the model you actually intend to ask.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
